            # Performs blocking file I/O on metadata
            
    def spawn_shell_pty(self):  # SYNCHRONOUS method
        with self._lock:
            # pty.openpty() - blocking
            # subprocess.Popen() - blocking
            # File writes to logs - blocking
```

WHY anyio.to_thread.run_sync DOESN'T FIX IT:

From [2025-11-07 16:30:00 UTC] investigation:
> "calling a blocking function like this from within an async WebSocket handler, 
> even with anyio.to_thread.run_sync, causes a deadlock or freezes the event loop 
> because the FrameworkShellManager is a stateful, non-thread-safe singleton."

The singleton pattern creates race conditions:
  1. Multiple async tasks call anyio.to_thread.run_sync(mgr.list_shells)
  2. Each runs in different thread from thread pool
  3. All threads access same FrameworkShellManager instance
  4. threading.RLock prevents simultaneous access
  5. Threads block waiting for lock
  6. Event loop has no async tasks to run (all blocked in threads)
  7. Deadlock or severe performance degradation

